inate  the global south as countries wait for a  vaccine  ground work is being done so health care  workers will be ready to get  shots in arms as fast as possible  crystal gavinson global news london  this is lebanon's lockdown still ahead  the rage of a nation in crisis  that is russian opposition leader alexei  navalny denouncing a court ruling that  rejected an appeal of his arrest  navalny told the court you won't succeed  in scaring tens of millions of people  who have been robbed by the government  he was taken into custody january 17th  when he returned from germany where he  spent five months recovering  from nerve agent poisoning he blames on  the kremlin  navalny's supporters are organizing  another round of mass protests across  russia  on sunday  police have been rounding up his  associates this doctor played the piano  while her apartment was raided today  navalny's wife and brother have also  been detained  people took to the streets in poland  tonight  angry about a court ruling which  effectively bans abortion  in october poland's highest court rule  terminating a pregnancy because of a  fetal defect is  unconstitutional abortion will now only  be permitted in cases of rape or incest  or when the mother's health or life is  in danger the french european affairs  minister tweeted today it is a reminder  rights can  recede if they are not defended  and in lebanon security forces fired  tear gas at protesters angry about  strict  lockdown measures and poor living  conditions this is the fourth straight  day of violence  at least one person was killed hundreds  of others injured  the unrest marks a major escalation in  frustration over the pandemic that is  worsening at an unprecedented  economic and financial time in lebanon a  surge in cases has triggered a  month-long  nationwide lockdown and around-the-clock  curfew pakistan's supreme court has  ruled four men convicted of kidnapping  and murdering american journalist  danielle pearl should be  freed the white house calls it an  affront to terrorism victims  everywhere ahmed omar saeed sheikh a  british national was considered the  ringleader in the 2002 kidnapping and  killing of pearl  pearl was the wall street journal south  asia bureau chief  assailants later filmed pearl's  beheading and sent the video to u.s  officials  in december a court ordered all four men  be set free  both the pearl family and pakistani  authorities appealed that decision and  today the supreme  court ruled against them the white house  is demanding pakistan review its legal  options  including allowing the united states to  prosecute sheikh  a team from the world health  organization has emerged from quarantine  now in wuhan china to begin work on  tracing the origins of covet 19.  they left their hotel to prepare for  field work and their first face-to-face  meeting with chinese scientists  the researchers plan to visit hospitals  labs and markets  and hope to speak with patients and  first responders  the fact-finding mission is politically  charged though china has avoided any  blame for alleged missteps in its early  response to the outbreak  the team is expected to stay in china  for two more weeks  the woes of wall street next the stock  market set up and the chat room where it  happened  you may have heard a lot of talk about  gamestop it's a david and goliath battle  between wall street's financial elite  and some small investors people have  banded together online to drive up the  stock price of gamestop a money losing  chain  of video game stores that company's  stock was trading for less than twenty  dollars a share  and then recently it began to soar as  investors snapped it up  on wednesday it closed at almost three  hundred and fifty dollars a share  jackson proskow explains how and why  this all happened  this was the week wall street got a run  for its money  social media average joes versus big  money players and guess what the army of  average joes are winning  so far those average joes have been on a  buying spree  snapping up shares of troubled companies  blackberry  amc theaters american airlines and the  big one  gamestop the struggling video game  retailer  i'm a blue collar investor right so i'm  i scrap all the time but now  when you get something like this it's  one of those all-in type things for days  the little guys have been cashing in  all while hedge funds lose billions it's  just a way of attacking wealthy people  and you know i think it's inappropriate  we all gotta work together and pull  together  you see unlike average investors big  hedge funds can actually profit from a  struggling business  it's called shorting if a stock price  drops they make  money but if the price rises they stand  to lose  that's where reddit's wall street bets  message board enters the story  when users saw hedge funds had bet  against gamestop and others  they banded together to buy shares  raising the price and reaping the  rewards  there is something to be said about the  fact that pretty much anybody can do it  too and watching them do it collectively  is certainly  certainly a show ironically this modern  day robin hood tale  also involves a stock trading app called  robinhood  which small investors used to snap up  all that shorted stock  but the hero turned villain as robin  hood and other brokerage sites  suddenly banned users from trading the  most volatile shares  shutting out anyone who wanted to cash  in amateur investors are really  necessary for  the health of the market so you want  them in the market  but you don't want them triggering  irrational results risky as their  investments may have been  those amateur investors turned the  financial world upside down  by finding a way to beat wall street at  its own game  jackson prosko global news washington  and that is global national for this  thursday i'm donna friesen  tonight's york canada is ottawa's reno  canal  it has opened for the first skate only  locals allowed though keeping in line  with ontario's pandemic restrictions  skaters have to wear face masks and for  now only a third of the canal is open  other sections are  will open once ice conditions are deemed  safe in a normal year about 1700  visitors take a trip on the beautiful  canal every day  thanks for watching robin gill will be  here tomorrow i'll see you on saturday  for the new reality  take care of yourselves bye-bye
 

